# name: Build fingerprint
# description: Rewrites userdebug to user in ro.build.fingerprint and strips custom-ROM names from it. OFF by default - read the warning below before enabling.
# enabled: 0

# WARNING, and the reason this ships disabled:
#   Stripping a ROM name out of a fingerprint leaves the rest behind,
#   so "lineage_a15x/..." becomes "_a15x/...". That is a malformed
#   fingerprint, and a malformed fingerprint is more suspicious than an
#   honest one - attestation compares it against Google's list of real
#   builds. The fork does the same thing; it is inherited behaviour,
#   not an improvement.
#
#   On a stock ROM none of these needles are present, so every rule
#   below is a no-op and enabling this changes nothing. It is only
#   worth turning on if you have checked what your fingerprint actually
#   becomes:
#       resetprop ro.build.fingerprint
#
# 'replace' rewrites a substring of the existing value and never
# creates the prop. Omitting the last field deletes the substring.
replace  ro.build.fingerprint  userdebug  user
replace  ro.build.fingerprint  evolution
replace  ro.build.fingerprint  crdroid
replace  ro.build.fingerprint  lineage
